red to trade Piramal Finance Ltd (PIRAMALFIN) on NSE?","answer":"Piramal Finance Ltd (PIRAMALFIN) is approved under SEBI's Margin Trading Facility (MTF) with an initial maintenance margin requirement of approximately 20%. This enables swing traders to access 5.0x purchasing power on eligible Indian brokerage platforms."},{"question":"What are the key moving average support and resistance levels for PIRAMALFIN?","answer":"Based on daily technical charting, PIRAMALFIN's short-term dynamic pullback support rests at its 20 EMA (\u20b91947.73), intermediate support at the 50 EMA (\u20b92034.38), and long-term institutional trend support at the 200 EMA (\u20b91933.11)."},{"question":"What are the daily pivot point support and resistance levels for PIRAMALFIN?","answer":"For the current trading session, PIRAMALFIN's central Pivot Point (PP) is \u20b91838.73. Immediate resistance levels are R1: \u20b91861.06 and R2: \u20b91887.13, while key downside support levels are S1: \u20b91812.66 and S2: \u20b91790.33."},{"question":"Which Indian broker provides the lowest MTF interest rate for PIRAMALFIN?","answer":"Kotak Neo currently offers the lowest headline MTF interest rate starting at 9.69% p.a. (\u20b926.55/day per \u20b91 Lakh borrowed), followed by m.Stock at 9.99% p.a., Dhan at 12.49% p.a., and Zerodha at 14.60% p.a."},{"question":"At what price does PIRAMALFIN trigger an MTF margin call or liquidation?","answer":"With a 20% initial margin, PIRAMALFIN has a safety buffer of approximately 16.5%. If the price falls to \u20b91532.22, your broker will issue a margin shortfall notice. Positions must also be authorized via CDSL/NSDL OTP pledge before 9:00 PM on T-day."}],"last_updated":"2026-10-30T06:59:32.852739Z"}